# UI Screenshot Verification (Hard Gate)

**Task is NOT complete** until screenshot verification passes for any user-visible change
(layout, spacing, typography, colors, copy, modals, overlays, responsive breakpoints).

## Required Before Final Response

1. Navigate to every affected route using the available browser or Playwright tool (seed auth/state if needed).
2. Capture a screenshot — desktop >=1280px; for grid/shell/column work also ~390px mobile.
3. Inspect the screenshot and fix regressions in the same session.
4. End with a `Screenshot-Check` line listing routes + viewports verified.

```
Screenshot-Check: /arena @1440px, @390px — header single-line, leaderboard readable.
```

## Blocked — Do Not Mark Done

- Unit/typecheck/doctor green alone is not enough.
- "Should work" without actually looking at a screenshot.
- Skipping after a browser error without attempting recovery (reload, seed state, evaluate).
- Omitting the Screenshot-Check line when UI files changed.

## When No Browser Tool Is Available

If no browser MCP or Playwright is available in the current environment, state this truthfully:
`Screenshot-Check: BLOCKED — no browser/Playwright available in this environment.`
Do NOT claim the check was performed. Mark the task incomplete for UI verification and hand off to the user or a capable agent.

## Layout/Grid Extra

After `col-span-*`, `@container`, `w-full`: confirm measured widths via evaluation or Playwright.

## Relationship to Ponytail

This gate is a minimum correctness requirement. Ponytail YAGNI does not apply here.
